name=HARMONIE - Lifestyle Audio Tune
id=HARMONIE_LifestyleAudioTune
description=Turns down "Lifestyle: Hobbies" (Workshop ID 3403870858) music and sound effects, which ship very loud and audible from very far away. Overrides the mod's disco/jukebox/DJ booth music, playable instruments (guitar, harmonica, etc.) and other equipment SFX (turn on/off, button presses, etc.) to half their original volume and a shared 25-tile max hearing distance (down from 75-100 tiles). Also adds a real in-game settings page (Options -> Mods -> HARMONIE: Lifestyle Audio Tune) with a live volume slider -- applies instantly, no restart -- covering the DJ Booth, Jukebox idle/chime sounds, instruments and equipment SFX. Also wires up 4 JoJo's Bizarre Adventure openings (Sono Chi no Sadame, Bloody Stream, Fighting Gold, Giorno's Theme), the "HEYYEYAAEYAAAEYAEYAA" meme song, and three more requested tracks (Bothnia - Someday I'll Wait, Violette Wautier - Wanna Be Yours, Honkai: Star Rail - What the Ripple Sees) as playable instrument tracks -- each song registered across every instrument that suits its real instrumentation (Electric Guitar, Bass, Acoustic Guitar, Saxophone, Trumpet, Keytar, Harmonica, Flute, Violin) via Lifestyle's own addon extension point -- audio files not included (copyrighted; see media/sound/README.txt), drop your own legally-obtained .ogg files in to enable. Must load after Lifestyle: Hobbies.
